<title>USA: U.S. June existing home sales fell 2.6 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. June existing home sales fell 2.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sales of existing U.S. homes fell 2.6 percent in June to a seasonally adjusted annual rate of 4.14 million units from a revised 4.25 million units in May, the National Association of Realtors said Friday.</p>
<p>Wall Street economists had forecast June sales of 4.19 million units.</p>
<p>The June sales rate was down 0.5 percent from sales of 4.16 million in June last year.</p>
<p>NAR reported the following details of existing home sales</p>
<p>in seasonally adjusted annual rates:</p>
<p> -				 June    May-(Prev)  June96</p>
<p> Units Sold (in millions)	4.14   4.25   4.24    4.16</p>
<p> -				 June    May-(Prev) June97/96</p>
<p> Units Sold, Pct Change    -2.6    4.7   4.4     -0.5</p>
<p> -				 June    May-(Prev)  June96</p>
<p> Median Price (1,000s)    127.2  123.1  123.2   122.9</p>
<p>Note--Median sales price is the midpoint where half the</p>
<p>homes sold for more and half for less.</p>
<p> -				 June    May-(Prev)  June96</p>
<p> Units Available (millions)    2.06   2.40   2.38    2.21</p>
<p> Months' Worth of Supply    6.0    6.8    6.7     6.4</p>
<p> FHLMC 30-Year Rate (Pct)  7.69   7.94   7.94    8.32</p>
<p>Note--FHLMC rate is the Federal Home Loan Mortgage Corp's</p>
<p>average commitment rate for 30-year fixed-rate mortgages.</p>
<p>Units Sold By Region, seasonally adjusted, in 1,000s:</p>
<p>    -	   June	  May--(Prev)     June96</p>
<p> Northeast    600.0     650.0    650.0     640.0</p>
<p> Midwest    1,080.0   1,070.0  1,070.0   1,010.0</p>
<p> South	1,580.0   1,580.0  1,580.0   1,570.0</p>
<p> West	   880.0     940.0    930.0     930.0</p>
<p>Median Price By Region, unadjusted, in 1,000s of dollars:</p>
<p>    -	   June	  May--(Prev)     June96</p>
<p> Northeast    146.9     146.5    146.6     146.1</p>
<p> Midwest	108.4     104.8    105.1     105.0</p>
<p> South	  112.6     108.1    108.3     106.8</p>
<p> West	   164.9     159.6    159.4     157.2</p>
<p>&quot;While there has been a slight tapering off, the market has remained strong, due to favorable economic conditions overall,&quot; NAR President Russell Booth said.</p>
</text>
